{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-callbacks_and_events-java-repair-01","problem":"Repair the implementation below.

`submit` synchronously scans `statements` and coordinates a `BatchListener` with a final `Completion` callback.

A statement is malformed when it is `null` or contains only whitespace. For each malformed statement, call `listener.onRejected(index, statement)` and exclude it from all batches. Accepted statements are delivered unchanged through `listener.onBatch` in batches of at most `batchSize`, preserving their input order. Deliver a final partial batch when necessary. After all batch and rejection callbacks have returned, call `completion.onComplete(accepted, rejected)` exactly once with the corresponding totals.

You may assume `statements`, `listener`, and `completion` are non-null and `batchSize` is positive. Callbacks execute synchronously and do not throw exceptions.

Return a corrected complete `Solution.java` source file using this exact API:

```java
public static void submit(String[] statements, int batchSize,
                          BatchListener listener, Completion completion)
```

Known-bad source:

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

public final class Solution {
    private Solution() {}

    public interface BatchListener {
        void onBatch(List<String> statements);
        void onRejected(int index, String statement);
    }

    public interface Completion {
        void onComplete(int accepted, int rejected);
    }

    public static void submit(String[] statements, int batchSize,
                              BatchListener listener, Completion completion) {
        List<String> batch = new ArrayList<>();
        int accepted = 0;
        int rejected = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < statements.length; i++) {
            String statement = statements[i];
            if (statement == null) {
                listener.onRejected(i, statement);
                rejected++;
                continue;
            }

            batch.add(statement);
            accepted++;
            if (batch.size() == batchSize) {
                listener.onBatch(batch);
                batch = new ArrayList<>();
            }
        }

        if (!batch.isEmpty()) {
            listener.onBatch(batch);
        }
        completion.onComplete(accepted, rejected);
    }
}
