","known_bad_label":"Records with an empty key are dispatched as valid entry events instead of malformed events."},{"id":"cap-v2-graph_and_tree-java-generation-01","problem":"Create a complete `Solution.java` implementation for this exact API:

```java
public static List<String> dependencyOrder(
        Map<String, List<String>> dependencies, String root)
```

`dependencies` describes a directed acyclic dependency graph. Each key is a component, and its list contains the components it directly depends on. Return exactly the components reachable from `root`, including `root`, with every dependency appearing before any component that depends on it.

The order must be deterministic: perform a depth-first traversal from `root`, visit each component's direct dependencies in ascending lexicographic order, append a component after visiting all of its dependencies, and append each component only once. The ordering of keys and lists in the supplied map must not affect the result.

You may assume `dependencies` and `root` are non-null, every referenced component is a key in the map, all dependency lists are non-null, and the graph is acyclic. Use only the Java standard library.","reference_code":"import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Map;
import java.util.Set;

public final class Solution {
    private Solution() {}

    public static List<String> dependencyOrder(
            Map<String, List<String>> dependencies, String root) {
        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();
        Set<String> visited = new HashSet<>();
        visit(root, dependencies, visited, result);
        return result;
    }

    private static void visit(String component,
                              Map<String, List<String>> dependencies,
                              Set<String> visited,
                              List<String> result) {
        if (!visited.add(component)) {
            return;
        }

        List<String> direct = new ArrayList<>(dependencies.get(component));
        direct.sort(String::compareTo);
        for (String dependency : direct) {
            visit(dependency, dependencies, visited, result);
        }
        result.add(component);
    }
}
